    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d727">

                <pb facs="0819" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg625"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 (Potsdam)/7–2045</note>
                <head>No. 727<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the United States
                        Delegation</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1945-07-20">July 20, 1945</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Declaration on Italy and
                        Spain</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Proposal Presented to Foreign
                        Ministers July</hi> 20, 1945<anchor n="1" xml:id="d727-f1"/></p>
                <p>In the statement on the policy toward Italy introduced by the President on July
                        17<anchor n="2" xml:id="d727-f2"/> we propose that there be included a
                    statement to the effect that the Three Heads of Government will support the
                    entry of Italy into the United Nations Organization.</p>
                <p>The Three Heads of Government further declare that they will not support the
                    entry of Spain into the United Nations Organization, so long as Spain is under
                    the control of the present regime in that country.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
